WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.076
Welcome to KI-PA-A plus: AI Literacy and Governance at the Power Academy.

2
00:00:05.076 --> 00:00:12.911
In the next few minutes, you'll see how this course works, how the three days run, and what you'll be able to do at the end.

3
00:00:13.711 --> 00:00:15.926
Here's a familiar moment.

4
00:00:15.926 --> 00:00:21.952
An AI assistant gives you a clear, confident answer, with a source.

5
00:00:21.952 --> 00:00:23.459
It sounds right.

6
00:00:23.459 --> 00:00:25.143
Do you pass it on?

7
00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:31.434
Knowing how a language model works won't answer that question for you.

8
00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:37.726
What helps is practice: checking, deciding, and taking responsibility.

9
00:00:37.726 --> 00:00:40.562
That's what this course trains.

10
00:00:41.362 --> 00:00:50.350
Every one of the twenty-four learning blocks lasts forty-five minutes and follows the same six phases.

11
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:54.667
Recall: you bring back what you learned earlier.

12
00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:59.073
Prompt: a short case, and your own first attempt.

13
00:00:59.073 --> 00:01:04.801
Explain: the trainer adds the core idea, in ten minutes at most.

14
00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:10.616
Apply: the longest phase, fifteen minutes of real work on a case.

15
00:01:10.616 --> 00:01:15.198
Compare: you check your result against a reference.

16
00:01:15.198 --> 00:01:20.133
And Secure: one exit answer, and your own if-then rule.

17
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:22.051
Why this order?

18
00:01:22.051 --> 00:01:24.510
Because research is quite clear.

19
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.565
Retrieving knowledge beats rereading it.

20
00:01:27.565 --> 00:01:32.408
Trying first, then comparing, sticks better than just listening.

21
00:01:32.408 --> 00:01:39.785
And concrete if-then plans make it more likely that you actually do something differently at work.

22
00:01:39.785 --> 00:01:43.138
So expect to think, write and discuss a lot.

23
00:01:43.138 --> 00:01:44.777
Mistakes are welcome.

24
00:01:44.777 --> 00:01:46.864
They're part of the method.

25
00:01:47.664 --> 00:01:50.143
The three days build on each other.

26
00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.409
Day one: understand and govern.

27
00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:59.776
How language models, RAG and agents work, where they fail, and how the EU AI Act sorts roles and risks.

28
00:01:59.776 --> 00:02:01.688
Day two: select and apply.

29
00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:09.550
The ISO 42001 management system, governance roles, the evaluation matrix, tool classes, and your own use case.

30
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.958
Day three: practice and transfer.

31
00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:16.066
Case cards, two role simulations, and your plan for work.

32
00:02:16.066 --> 00:02:22.795
Each day runs from nine to five, with eight blocks, breaks, and a short reflection at the end.

33
00:02:23.595 --> 00:02:28.815
Each day ends with a whole task that brings everything together.

34
00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.669
Day one: is it AI, and who are we?

35
00:02:31.669 --> 00:02:34.198
Day two: a tool decision memo.

36
00:02:34.198 --> 00:02:36.971
Day three: your decision dossier.

37
00:02:36.971 --> 00:02:40.886
These are real work products, not quiz answers.

38
00:02:41.686 --> 00:02:45.057
By the end, you'll be able to do four things.

39
00:02:45.057 --> 00:02:50.300
Understand: explain what an AI system does, and where its limits are.

40
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:55.394
Classify: place a situation in the AI Act's roles and risk classes.

41
00:02:55.394 --> 00:02:58.840
Select: compare tools against clear criteria.

42
00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:06.106
And take responsibility: decide to proceed, pause or stop, with reasons, oversight and an owner.

43
00:03:06.106 --> 00:03:13.297
Running through all of it is calibrated trust: trusting AI as much as it deserves, and no more.

44
00:03:14.097 --> 00:03:19.629
On day one, you start with a short judgement check and your personal learning contract.

45
00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:26.115
On day three, you take a parallel check with twelve new situations, so you can see your own progress.

46
00:03:26.115 --> 00:03:28.404
It's a reflection aid, not an exam.

47
00:03:28.404 --> 00:03:35.017
And you'll leave with your decision record, a transfer plan, and a thirty, sixty, ninety day follow-up.

48
00:03:35.817 --> 00:03:37.148
Two ground rules.

49
00:03:37.148 --> 00:03:43.960
Use synthetic or cleared material only: no personal, confidential or operational data.

50
00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.388
And bring your real questions.

51
00:03:46.388 --> 00:03:53.827
In the next tutorial, you'll see how the training website supports you through all three days.

52
00:03:53.827 --> 00:03:55.628
See you in the course.
